      "S3",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 53,
    "html": "<p>Charles M. Pigott was an American industrialist who led PACCAR, the truck manufacturer established by his grandfather. A Stanford-trained engineer and former naval pilot, he developed the family business into an international producer of Kenworth and Peterbilt trucks. His career combined substantial company ownership with three decades of leadership before retiring in 1997.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "A closed Scout camp in Washington became a practical project for Charles M. Pigott, the former PACCAR chief. He raised funds to reopen the site near Lake Hughes, which took his name. Scouting connected his childhood to his civic work: an Eagle Scout as a teenager, he eventually served as national president of the organisation.\n\nAt Seattle University, Pigott helped establish scholarships covering tuition, housing, food and fees for students arriving from Catholic and Jesuit schools. He also endowed the leadership of its expanded College of Nursing and Health Sciences. The expanded college brought nursing together with kinesiology and introduced a women's-health focus for advanced nursing students.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full university memorial directly establishes camp fundraising, scholarships and the endowed deanship; family obituary independently confirms national Scouting leadership."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2"
    ],
    "word_count": 107,
    "html": "<p>A closed Scout camp in Washington became a practical project for Charles M. Pigott, the former PACCAR chief. He raised funds to reopen the site near Lake Hughes, which took his name. Scouting connected his childhood to his civic work: an Eagle Scout as a teenager, he eventually served as national president of the organisation.</p>\r\n<p>At Seattle University, Pigott helped establish scholarships covering tuition, housing, food and fees for students arriving from Catholic and Jesuit schools. He also endowed the leadership of its expanded College of Nursing and Health Sciences. The expanded college brought nursing together with kinesiology and introduced a women's-health focus for advanced nursing students.</p>\r\n"
  },
